  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y=x+\\frac{1}{x} \\text { or } \\frac{d y}{d x}=1-\\frac{1}{x^2}$\nFor $\\max$. or $\\min ., 1-\\frac{1}{x^2}=0 \\Rightarrow x=\\pm 1$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}^2 \\mathrm{y}}{\\mathrm{dx}^2}=\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{x}^3} \\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}^2 \\mathrm{y}}{\\mathrm{dx}^2}\\right)_{\\mathrm{x}=2}=2(+$ ve minima)\nTherefore $x=1$",
    "image": null
